<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tuscarora people</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tuscarora Nation</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tuscarora are an Iroquoian people originally from the coastal plain of North Carolina. After their defeat by colonists in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuscarora-war">Tuscarora War</a> of 1711–1713, most moved north and around 1722 were adopted into the Iroquois Confederacy under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oneida-people">Oneida</a> sponsorship, which then became the Six Nations. Many supported the Americans in the Revolution, and today they live on the Tuscarora Reservation near Niagara Falls and at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/six-nations-of-the-grand-river">Six Nations of the Grand River</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tuscarora-people.jpg" alt="Tuscarora people" width="320" height="389" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: George Catlin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:George_Catlin_-_C%C3%BA-sick,_Son_of_the_Chief_-_1985.66.271_-_Smithsonian_American_Art_Museum.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>When the <b>Tuscarora</b> moved north from North Carolina after the Tuscarora War of 1711–1713 and were adopted around 1722, they joined under the sponsorship of the Oneida, and the league became the Six Nations.</blockquote><a href="/empire/iroquois-confederacy">Iroquois Confederacy · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>Today the <b>Tuscarora Nation</b> lives near Lewiston, New York, and at Six Nations of the Grand River in Ontario.</blockquote><a href="/state/tuscarora-nation">Tuscarora Nation</a></li></ul></section>
